      "message": "Looking at phaser, the i2c port configuration matches yorp, and that really seems like a function of which EC is used.\n\nWe can pull this into board.c but it will be the same copy everywhere (so I lean towards keeping it here). However, if we do need one board variant to be different, I plan on making a OCTOPUS_I2C_CUSTOM_PORT option (or something like that) that complies out the definition from baseboard and would rely on board.c to define the i2c_port_t variable.\n\nI don\u0027t want to hack baseboard.c up with a bunch of variant specific code, but I think it is reasonable if it contains the two main variants of each component (2 ecs, 2 typec, 2, chargers, etc)",
