      "side": 1,
      "message": "For static structures I don\u0027t see why it\u0027s necessary to have them in one file. If one wants to compare two files can be opened side-by-side? \n\nIn general this sets a bad precedent where everything is getting thrown into a single file and sprinkling #ifdefs around. There is more than one way to share code.\n\nYes, these port layouts can be shared and are a function of 1. EC used and 2. following specific ref design. However, that determination is pretty easy to do in a build.mk proper saying \"use this .c\" file. btw, my name suggestions weren\u0027t real. You can name them according to ec type. I was just using that as an example of two separate compilation units.",
